{
  "task_id": "dynamic-object-aware-egomotion",
  "top_k": 5,
  "requirements": [
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_c976945a87170a7e50d2",
      "requirement_type": "ARTIFACT",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/dynamic-object-aware-egomotion/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 1,
        "line_end": 1,
        "exact_text": "Given a video file /root/input.mp4, help me to analyze the camera motion (egomotion) and detect dynamic objects in this video. You need to give me 2 files: \n",
        "source_sha256": "b07a0726a27cb1549acb0c6cd750a3f909d3a1c4c0f6138eb6bb38270c4dee53",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_78d1f73c0327f7ad063b",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/dynamic-object-aware-egomotion/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 2,
        "line_end": 9,
        "exact_text": "1. A json file named /root/pred_instructions.json, it should record the mapping frame intervals to motion labels (valid labels: Stay, Dolly In, Dolly Out, Pan Left, Pan Right, Tilt Up, Tilt Down, Roll Left, Roll Right). The format is \n{\n  \"0->1\": [\n    \"Pan Right\"\n  ],\n  ...\n}\nin json file 0 stands for the start sample index, and 1 is the end sample index.\n",
        "source_sha256": "b07a0726a27cb1549acb0c6cd750a3f909d3a1c4c0f6138eb6bb38270c4dee53",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_cc88ebf913a257360269",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/dynamic-object-aware-egomotion/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 10,
        "line_end": 11,
        "exact_text": "2. A file stores a binary mask for each sampled frame, called /root/pred_dyn_masks.npz. The mask resolution is stored under the key \"shape\" as [H, W]. For each frame i, we store the binary mask in CSR sparse format using three keys: f_{i}_data, f_{i}_indices, and f_{i}_indptr. This CSR representation records the locations of True pixels (i.e., which columns are True in each row) instead of saving the full H×W dense mask.\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "b07a0726a27cb1549acb0c6cd750a3f909d3a1c4c0f6138eb6bb38270c4dee53",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    }
  ],
